# A program, invented by the future.
#
# The messages are not numbers this time: the future sends a whole 3-instruction program.
# The program is checked against every 8-bit input, and a candidate that gets even one of
# them wrong edits its own first instruction, so that timeline cannot be the message that
# was sent. What survives is a program that is correct on all 256 inputs.
#
# Spec: for every a in 0..255, end with t == 3 * a (8-bit arithmetic, so it wraps).
# Instruction set (op is the whole instruction):
#   0: t = t + a      1: t = t << 1     2: t = t ^ a     3: t = t + 1     4: t = t - a
# Start: t = 0. Three instructions. That is 5^3 = 125 candidate programs.
bits 8
prog = future(prog, 3)
bad = 0
for i in range(256):
    a = i
    t = 0
    for k in range(3):
        op = prog[k]
        if op < 0 or op > 4:
            bad = 1
        if op == 0:
            t = t + a
        elif op == 1:
            t = t << 1
        elif op == 2:
            t = t ^ a
        elif op == 3:
            t = t + 1
        elif op == 4:
            t = t - a
    if t != a * 3:
        bad = 1
if bad != 0:
    prog[0] = prog[0] + 1
show prog[0]
show prog[1]
show prog[2]
